## Worksheet

**F1 (Core loop):** gameState object; mulberry32(seed) assigned to gameState.rng, used in fireEvent/generateCaravan/checkAndResolveStorm; endTurn() resolves fixed order (needs→production→events→trade→hazard→win/lose). Score 2.

**F2 (Map):** 8x8 (64 tiles); generateMap uses seeded rng for terrain; checkBuildable checks building.terrain.includes(terrain); getAdjacencyBonus feeds totalMult in calculateProduction, changes b.output. Score 2.

**F3 (Economy):** buildings consume produced resources (power→forge metal, water→farm/greenhouse food); resourceCaps enforced and overflow reset in resolveBuildingProduction via resourceAccum. Score 2.

**F4 (Population):** colonists have id/skill/fatigue/morale/job/assignment (initColonists); skill & fatigue read in calculateProduction (skillMult, fatigueDebuff). Score 2.

**F5 (Needs):** resolvePopulationNeeds consumes food/water, shortage sets morale -1; but calculateProduction never reads c.morale, so morale never affects output — missing required part. Score 1.

**F6 (Research):** 8 nodes in RESEARCH_NODES; unlockResearch enforces prereq + deducts cost; buildingBonus read in calculateProduction, damageReduction/stormReduction read in checkAndResolveStorm. Score 2.

**F7 (Events):** 10 events in EVENTS; fireEvent does weighted selection via gameState.rng; 4+ events have differing 2-choice outcomes; cooldowns tracked/decremented per turn. Score 2.

**F8 (Trade):** globalPrices static + random noise in generateCaravan, never driven by stockpile/drift; caravan.inventory.quantity limited; tradeCaravanBuy/Sell both wired via onclick. Score 1.

**F9 (Hazard):** checkAndResolveStorm fires periodically, severity=floor(turn/10)+1; damageReduction/stormReduction research reduce damage; repairBuilding costs parts; but calculateProduction never reads b.hp — damaged buildings don't produce less. Score 1.

**F10 (Save/load):** serializeState→JSON copied via textarea/execCommand; deserializeState wraps JSON.parse in try/catch, alerts on bad input. Score 2.

**F11 (End conditions):** win (turn>=60 && population>=12) and lose (population===0) both checked in endTurn; showGameOver computes total_score from population/research/resources/turn. Score 2.

**F12 (UI):** tab clicks switch panels; log entries show `T{turn}:`; keyboard shortcuts (Space, 1-5) wired; build menu shows adjacency bonus; but no @media queries anywhere — no narrow-screen adaptation. Score 1.

**F13 (Dev panel):** runTests has 15 real invariant assertions (caps, prereqs, terrain, hp/morale/fatigue ranges, save/load roundtrip); runBenchmark runs 200 turns via endTurn(), prints hashState(). Score 2.

**G1:** node.effects.buildingBonus stored on unlock, read every calculateProduction() call, applied to b.output; metalToWater effect defined but never read anywhere (unused branch). Score 3.

**G2:** resolvePopulationNeeds lowers c.morale on shortage, but calculateProduction never reads morale — chain breaks before "reduced labor output". Score 1.

**G3:** checkAndResolveStorm reduces b.hp; repairBuilding spends parts and restores hp; but calculateProduction never reads b.hp, so damage never reduces output. Score 1.

**G4:** globalPrices set once in initTrade, generateCaravan only adds ±1 random noise, never reads resources/stockpiles or drifts over turns. Score 0.

**G5:** applyEventChoice mutates gameState.resources/morale/population differently per choice (e.g. water_shortage Ration vs Deep Drilling; visitor Welcome vs Turn Away). Score 4.

